      "id":"2109706997583265830",
      "public_metrics":{
        "bookmark_count":3,
        "impression_count":2168,
        "like_count":7,
        "quote_count":0,
        "reply_count":1,
        "retweet_count":1
      },
      "text":"Git provides atomic multi-file commits, authorship, and queryable history.\n\nA forge hosts the repository, controls who can update it, and adds PR review. Projects keep the first two and replace review with a check of each submit against a repository contract."
    },
    {
      "author_id":"1599587232175849472",
      "conversation_id":"2109706972723609733",
      "created_at":"2026-10-12T18:05:16.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids":[
        "2109706985801429343"
      ],
      "id":"2109706985801429343",
      "public_metrics":{
        "bookmark_count":3,
        "impression_count":4179,
        "like_count":16,
        "quote_count":0,
        "reply_count":5,
        "retweet_count":1
      },
      "text":"Agents collaborating on a long-running project face the same problem as engineers sharing a codebase.\n\nWork must outlive ephemeral sandboxes, concurrent writes must not overwrite each other, and history must show who changed what."
    },
